  "note": "Concept names and slot fields (axis/button/negate/type) are read directly from a real Battlefield 6 PROFSAVE_profile (GstKeyBinding.infantry.<Concept>.<slot>.<field>) - not sourced from another Battlefield title. Frostbite's binding scheme is NOT stable across titles: Battlefield 4's own documented type-code meaning ('0=keyboard, 1=joystick axis, 2=joystick button') directly contradicts what BF6 actually uses, confirmed by testing - do not borrow another title's table again. type 2 (keyboard) bindings were cross-referenced against a live BF6 install's real Edit Key Bindings menu (5 independent matches: Big Map=M, Quick Loadout Customization=Y, Interact/Quick Upgrade=E, Toggle Inventory/Scoreboard=Tab, Enter/Exit Vehicle=E) against the public, standard DirectInput DIK_* scan code table - a Microsoft API standard, not Frostbite-specific, so it is not expected to drift between BF6 patches the way an internal enum might. type 0/1 (mouse) and type 3/4 (controller, unconfirmed which) are NOT decoded - shown as raw values. Concept labels marked confirmed:true were read directly off the in-game menu during that same cross-reference; the rest are inferred from the concept's own internal name (self-descriptive, e.g. ConceptJump -> Jump) and have NOT been individually verified against the menu - shown for reference, same honesty bar as this project's confidence:unverified settings elsewhere.",
